  },
  "executionSupported": false,
  "pilotReady": false,
  "liveAdmissionAllowed": false,
  "implementationVerified": false,
  "receiptCrossFieldRules": [
    "Canonical JSON rejects duplicates, floats, non-ASCII, unknown/missing fields; payload hash excludes envelope hash and seals. Verify all three unique role signatures over domain string plus payload hash, using out-of-band pinned role/build keys; input never supplies trust.",
    "Nonce/request/attempt/generation match the prepared request, fresh within 30 seconds with bounded clock error; unknown clock denies. Each role acknowledges the same profile contract and builds bound to official release qualification. A daemon version is not driver binary identity.",
    "Exact image reference suffix equals platform manifest digest, config/layer closure and observed OS/architecture match the qualified request. Native Linux WSL/Desktop values are literal not-applicable; WSL requires exact qualified versions. Unknown platform denies.",
    "Fixture matches approved path/type/mode/owner/size/hash/nlink and immutable image membership and final namespace object. argv[0] equals fixture.path; argv/cwd/uid/gid equal request and verified image identity. No symlink/hardlink race or post-seal mutation.",
    "All child mount rows are read-only, visibleToChild true and private propagation; supervisor-only rows are not visible or reachable by child. Enumerate both complete mount namespaces, including stacked and automatic mounts. Derive counts and table hashes, never trust declared zero.",
    "Every writable supervisor row is private-tmpfs with positive byte/inode ceilings within aggregate limits; every child-visible backing is immutable and contains no control material. Mount RO alone does not exclude writable device semantics; block writable devices and proc-root escape.",
    "Exact FD numbers are 0 read, 1 write, 2 write, unique dedicated nonblocking anonymous pipes; no other descriptor exists at workload exec. Trusted setup/barrier descriptors must be consumed and closed, with independent final observation tied to the sealed instance.",
    "Policy post-loader snapshot and installed rules must be supplied through authenticated evidence and hash-verified; semantic projection equals the approved policy including empty RW/network/provider groups. Never substitute authored policy hash or RF041 source projection for observed runtime hash.",
    "Enforced memorySwapBytes equals memoryBytes; all requested finite limits match observation. Total capture bounds all child/control diagnostic streams without payload leakage, stderr budget zero for v3; any unknown enforcement denies.",
    "Payload and all evidence are sealed against mutation until single-use acknowledgement and exec; receipt expiry, cancellation, crash, update or failed cleanup invalidates generation. No cached receipt, partial success or retry into retained mutable state.",
    "Mount rows are sorted by namespace, namespaceGeneration and mountId; FD rows by number; seals by role. Duplicate IDs, unknown flag semantics, overmount gaps or truncated evidence deny. Mount table hash covers canonical rows, policy hashes identify exact canonical authenticated evidence bytes."
  ],
  "v3TestLimits": {
    "cpuMillis": 1000,
    "memoryBytes": 536870912,
    "memorySwapBytes": 536870912,
    "pids": 64,
    "setupTimeoutMs": 30000,
